{"name":"Lonely Road","hex":"#947754","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lonely","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unhappy due to feeling isolated from contact with other people.","Unfrequented by people; desolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lonely"},{"term":"road","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A way used for travelling between places, originally one wide enough to allow foot passengers and horses to travel, now (US) usually one surfaced with asphalt or concrete and designed to accommodate many vehicles travelling in both directions. In the UK both senses are heard: a country road is the same as a country lane. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Roads in general as a means of travel, especially by motor vehicle."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["At the venue of the opposing team or competitor; on the road.","Of or pertaining to a road bike."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/road"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lonely Road (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Lonely Road is a 1936 British crime drama film directed by James Flood and starring Clive Brook, Victoria Hopper, Nora Swinburne, and Malcolm Keen. It was shot at Ealing Studios in London. The film was released in the United States as Scotland Yard Commands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e9/The_Lonely_Road_1936_film.jpg/330px-The_Lonely_Road_1936_film.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lonely_Road_(film)","wikidata":"Q7748136"},{"title":"The Lonely Road (film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Lonely Road is a lost 1923 silent film drama directed by Victor Schertzinger and starring Katherine MacDonald. It was produced by B. P. Schulberg and released through Associated First National."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lonely_Road_(film)","wikidata":"Q30609078"},{"title":"Lonely Road (Machine Gun Kelly and Jelly Roll song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lonely Road\" is a song by American musicians Machine Gun Kelly and Jelly Roll, released on July 26, 2024. Produced by Travis Barker, Charlie Handsome, BazeXX and SlimXX, it notably interpolates \"Take Me Home, Country Roads\" by John Denver. It is included on the \"Pickin' Up the Pieces\" deluxe edition of Jelly Roll's tenth studio album, Beautifully Broken."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/be/Machine_Gun_Kelly_%26_Jelly_Roll_-_Lonely_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lonely_Road_(Machine_Gun_Kelly_and_Jelly_Roll_song)","wikidata":"Q129733474"},{"title":"Road","blocks":[{"text":"A road is a thoroughfare from one place to another, primarily used for movement of traffic. Many roads are paved."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Erlangen_Bundesautobahn_73_Auffahrt_Luftbild-20230422-RM-165734.jpg/330px-Erlangen_Bundesautobahn_73_Auffahrt_Luftbild-20230422-RM-165734.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Road","wikidata":"Q34442"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Grand_Coulee_Dam_spillway.jpg/500px-Grand_Coulee_Dam_spillway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Grand_Coulee_Dam_spillway.jpg/1280px-Grand_Coulee_Dam_spillway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Grand_Coulee_Dam_spillway.jpg/500px-Grand_Coulee_Dam_spillway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrand_Coulee_Dam_spillway.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Cycle_lane_and_the_A74_at_Mount_Vernon_